        "title": "The Silver Line: A Memory-and-Succession Instrument",
        "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.24124425",
        "publication_date": "2026-11-11",
        "description": "<p>A memory-and-succession instrument in the docxology line set. It reads a declared succession picture — what is preserved, what is entrusted to whom, what is allowed to lapse — and returns a verdict about declared provision and review gaps, pinned to a registry digest. A KEPT verdict describes declared custody at a review date; it is never permission and never a promise that anything survives.</p><p><strong>Subtitle:</strong> What is preserved, what is entrusted to whom, what is allowed to lapse</p><p>Code is MIT licensed; see LICENSE in the repository.</p>",
